# Data and provenance

- One observation is one result for one context, composition, condition and method run.
- Use liquid-gas, liquid-liquid, three-phase-contact, adsorption, bulk, dispersion and porous-media contexts.
- Distinguish equilibrium surface tension, equilibrium IFT and dynamic tension.
- Preserve raw text, original value and unit; add canonical value, unit and versioned conversion separately.
- For liquid-liquid IFT, record both phase compositions when available.
- For contact angle, require droplet, ambient phase, surface, geometry and measured-through phase.
- For dynamic data, require a series coordinate and time origin; zero surface age is valid.
- Store temperature, pressure, pH, salinity basis, dissolved gas and equilibration state when reported.
- Store method, instrument or software version, uncertainty, repeats and exact source locator.
- Separate experiment/MD/QM/continuum/correlation/ML origin from publication/database ingestion route.
- Every transformation records input hash, code or prompt version, agent and timestamp.
- Do not overwrite raw inputs. Derived outputs go to a later data stage.
